===Etymology===
1) From {{etyl|it}} slang {{term|fugazi||fake|lang=it}}; perhaps also slang version of ''fugacious'' derived from {{etyl|la}} ''fugac-'', stem of {{term|fugax|fugāx|ready to flee, flying|lang=la}}, hence, fleeting, transitory.

2) Acronym: '''F'''ucked '''U'''p, '''G'''ot '''A'''mbushed, '''Z'''ipped '''I'''n (a body bag).  Describes process of dying in combat in the Vietnam War.

